@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what docker/sandbox-templates actually ships, measured from the registry
' covers: defs/base/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/base/proveo-harden
' Lineage and tagging: image-lineage-and-publish.puml (same directory).
' Why the rebase happened: _spec/_plans/image-size-reduction.puml (Cut 4).
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── AUTHORITATIVE SOURCES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   templates   : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/templates/
'   customize   : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/
'   shell agent : https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/agents/shell/
'   tags        : https://hub.docker.com/r/docker/sandbox-templates/tags
'   quickstart  : https://github.com/dockersamples/sbx-quickstart
'
' ── THE RULE WE WERE BREAKING ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' "Custom templates are reusable sandbox images that EXTEND ONE OF THE BUILT-IN
' agent environments with additional tools and configuration baked in."
' proveo/base descended from debian:trixie-slim instead, so it inherited none of
' what a sandbox is assumed to carry. Everything below was then re-derived by
' hand, and the docker half was re-derived WRONG — see Cut 4.
'
' ── MEASURED FROM THE REGISTRY, 2026-09-06 ──────────────────────────────────
' docker/sandbox-templates:shell-docker-0.5.0, linux/arm64, config blob read
' directly (no daemon needed): auth.docker.io token -> registry-1.docker.io
' manifest -> config blob; layers listed with `tar -tzv` off the blob stream.
'
'   base       ubuntu:questing (26.04)
'   USER       agent
'   WORKDIR    /home/agent/workspace
'   ENTRYPOINT ["tini", "--"]     CMD ["bash"]
'   LABEL      com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker = true   <- ALREADY SET
'   ENV        PATH includes /home/agent/.local/bin and
'              /usr/local/share/npm-global/bin
'              NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX=/usr/local/share/npm-global
'              NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1,172.17.0.0/16
'              BASH_ENV=/etc/sandbox-persistent.sh
'
'   IDENTITY   agent:x:1000:1000::/home/agent:/bin/bash
'              docker:x:1001:agent
'              sudo:x:27:agent
'              /etc/sudoers.d/agent -> "agent ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL"
'   Every one of those four lines is something a proveo def CONSTRUCTS BY HAND
'   today, down to the docker group landing on gid 1001. The uid dance in
'   defs/*/Dockerfile is not wrong; on this base it is redundant.
'
'   TOOLING    git gh jq rg tini docker(CLI, 43 MB) sudo.ws uv curl
'              go 1.26, node, npm, python3.14, java 25
'   ENGINE     dockerd 102 MB, containerd 40 MB, runc 11 MB, docker-proxy 3 MB
'              (the -docker suffix is what carries these; plain tags have the
'               CLI only, and a CLI with no daemon is the mistake Cut 4 made)
'   SIZE       588.7 MB compressed across 15 layers
'
' ── THE SETUID TRAP, AND IT IS OURS ─────────────────────────────────────────
' The template ships exactly three setuid/setgid files:
'     -rwxr-sr-x  usr/bin/ssh-agent
'     -rwsr-xr-x  usr/bin/sudo.ws            <- /usr/bin/sudo resolves here
'     -rwsr-xr-x  usr/lib/openssh/ssh-keysign
' proveo-harden runs `find -perm -4000 -exec chmod u-s`, so on this base it
' DISARMS SUDO — and sudo is the agent user's only route to root. That is the
' shape of the failure the claudecode record left open at "what remains is the
' privilege": dockerd answering "Permission denied (you must be root)". That
' record concluded "proveo-harden is not implicated"; it was measured on a base
' with no sudo to strip, so the test was never like-for-like. sudo is now
' exempt by name in proveo-harden. ssh-agent and ssh-keysign stay stripped:
' neither is a privilege the harness uses, and keeping the cut narrow keeps the
' posture change to the one binary that had to change.
'
' ── WHAT THE REBASE DOES NOT CHANGE ─────────────────────────────────────────
' The per-def rename (agent -> claude/cursor/opencode/cecli, home symlinked back
' to /home/agent) STAYS. defs/claudecode/tests/test_workspace.sh asserts both
' halves — "HOME is /home/agent" and "/home/claude resolves to /home/agent" — so
' collapsing it to the template's bare `agent` would be a one-line change that
' reddens the suite. It is redundant on this base, not harmful.
'
' ── WHAT THE FIRST BUILD ATTEMPT TAUGHT ────────────────────────────────────
' The rebase was committed unbuilt — there is no daemon in a proveo sandbox,
' which is the finding that prompted the rebase — and the first real build on
' the host failed immediately. Recorded because each of these costs a full
' rebuild cycle to rediscover:
'
'   ARG SCOPE.  `ARG SANDBOX_TEMPLATE=...` sat between the builder stage and the
'     runtime stage. An ARG written AFTER a FROM belongs to THAT STAGE, so only a
'     declaration above EVERY FROM reaches a FROM line. buildx warned
'     "UndefinedArgInFrom" and failed with "base name should not be blank". The
'     contract test asserted the ARG EXISTED and passed on a Dockerfile that
'     could not build — existence was never the rule. It now asserts ORDER, for
'     every ARG any FROM interpolates, across all four base images.
'
'   NODESOURCE.  base-node installed Node from NodeSource, which publishes PER
'     UBUNTU RELEASE. The template's floor is ubuntu:questing (26.04) and moves
'     with the template, so that layer depended on a third party having packaged
'     whatever release the template happens to ship. Node now arrives as the
'     official nodejs.org tarball, pinned and sha256-verified, exactly as mise,
'     bun and plantuml already do. The test that pinned the NodeSource apt line
'     pinned a MECHANISM; it now pins the property — one Node, by version and
'     digest, verified after install.
'
'   xz AND GLOBS.  `tar -J` shells out to xz, which the template is not
'     guaranteed to carry, so xz-utils is installed BEFORE the extract rather
'     than in the same apt call after it. GNU tar matches --exclude against the
'     WHOLE member name, so `--exclude=CHANGELOG.md` never matched
'     `node-vX-linux-arm64/CHANGELOG.md`; the patterns are anchored `*/` now.
'
'   INHERITED WORKDIR.  The template sets WORKDIR /home/agent/workspace, and
'     BuildKit RECREATES a missing working directory before every RUN. The defs
'     rename uid 1000 and move /home/agent aside in one RUN, so the workdir
'     underneath reappeared before the next one and the move back died with
'     "usermod: directory /home/agent exists" (exit 12). The Debian base carried
'     no WORKDIR, so `/` is what this lineage always had; base declares it now,
'     and the four defs additionally rmdir an empty stub before moving. rmdir,
'     never rm -rf: a stub is empty, and a real home must fail loudly instead of
'     being silently discarded. Exercised against all three cases — stub,
'     idempotent re-run, and real content — before shipping.
'
'   A TEST THAT MEASURED THE WRONG THING, AGAIN.  The workdir test sliced the
'     runtime stage with an UNANCHORED search for "FROM ${SANDBOX_TEMPLATE}",
'     which matches the phrase where it appears inside a COMMENT near the top of
'     the file. "The runtime stage" therefore spanned the builder too, whose
'     WORKDIR /src satisfied the assertion no matter what the runtime stage
'     said: the test passed with the defect reintroduced. Anchored to `(?m)^FROM`
'     now. Third time in this rebase that a green test was measuring its own
'     setup rather than the contract — the tell each time was a negative check
'     that produced NO failure.
'
'   RESOLVE, DO NOT NAME.  `test -u /usr/bin/sudo.ws` hardcoded an alternatives
'     name, and `command -v java` assumed java was on PATH. Both now resolve the
'     real path and fail with a sentence naming what was missing, because a
'     build that dies on `test -x` prints nothing an operator can act on.
'
' Verified statically, since this sandbox still has no daemon: every apt package
' exists on questing (queried), both node tarball URLs resolve, and Playwright
' 1.61.0's own dependency table lists ubuntu26.04 — so `--with-deps` has a
' distro entry for the new floor.
'
' ── STILL OPEN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Whether the RENAMED user needs its own sudo grant. The template grants
' NOPASSWD:ALL to `agent` by name; after the rename that name belongs to a
' recreated uid-1000 user, so the grant survives while the working user
' (claude/cursor/cecli) has none. Our images shipped NO sudo at all until now,
' so granting one is a posture change and is the operator's call, not a
' packaging detail. Nothing is known to need it yet: sbx starts the daemon
' itself and does not invoke dockerd through the agent's sudo (scoped sudo was
' tried and changed nothing, byte-identical error).
' ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

title sandbox-template rebase — what the supported base already carries

component "docs: custom templates\n\"extend one of the built-in\"" as DOCS <<cloud>>
component "docker/sandbox-templates\nshell-docker-0.5.0" as TPL <<cloud>>

node "what it carries" as CARRY <<host>> {
  component "identity\nagent:1000 · docker:1001 · sudo" as ID <<app>>
  component "engine\ndockerd containerd runc proxy" as ENG <<app>>
  component "toolchain\ngo node python java git gh" as TOOL <<app>>
}

component "proveo/base\nwas debian:trixie-slim" as BASE <<app>>
component "hand-built identity\nre-derived, and docker re-derived wrong" as HAND <<error>>
component "proveo-harden\nchmod u-s on every setuid file" as HARD <<error>>
component "sudo.ws\nthe agent's only route to root" as SUDO <<db>>

DOCS ARROW_MAIN TPL : the supported base
TPL ARROW_MAIN ID
TPL ARROW_MAIN ENG
TPL ARROW_MAIN TOOL
TPL ARROW_MAIN BASE : rebased onto this
BASE ARROW_QUEUE HAND : what the old base made us write
HARD ARROW_ERROR SUDO : stripped the setuid bit
SUDO ARROW_QUEUE ENG : privilege the daemon needed

note bottom of TPL
  **The `-docker` suffix is the whole product.**
  Plain tags carry the client and no daemon, so a
  sandbox built on one answers `docker` and then
  fails to connect — the same half-provisioning
  Cut 4 arrived at from the other direction.
end note

note bottom of ID
  **Four lines we were writing by hand.** uid 1000
  named agent, home /home/agent, a docker group on
  gid 1001, and NOPASSWD sudo — our defs construct
  each one, matching gid 1001 by coincidence
  rather than by inheriting it.
end note

note bottom of HARD
  **The harden pass disarms sudo on this base.** A
  blanket chmod u-s takes the setuid bit off
  sudo.ws, which is the agent user's only route to
  root, so hardening and privilege collided in the
  one binary nobody had measured.
end note

note bottom of SUDO
  **Named in the old record, then acquitted.** It
  was cleared on a base that shipped no sudo, so
  the comparison was never like-for-like — the
  acquittal measured an absence rather than the
  binary it was meant to exonerate.
end note

note bottom of BASE
  **A base off the supported path pays twice.** It
  re-derives what the template gives, and it gets
  no correction when a re-derivation is wrong —
  which is how four manifests came to promise a
  daemon that no image carried.
end note

@enduml
